1
00:00:02,230 --> 00:00:07,860
So then, which one of you is my foe?

2
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:14,740
Raven Black Hero!
I am Evileye, of the Blue Rose!

3
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:19,890
As a fellow adamantite class adventurer,
I request that we party up!

4
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:24,250
Wait, what's the point 
of asking for his help?

5
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:26,710
I can't very well let <i>his</i> life be taken, too.

6
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:27,990
Understood.

7
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:37,050
May I begin by asking your name, please?

8
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:40,640
My name is Jaldabaoth.

9
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:46,770
Jaldabaoth? Well, all right. I am Momon,

10
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:49,490
adamantite class adventurer.

11
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:52,500
What is your purpose here?

12
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:57,450
It seems that a mighty item that can
summon us and make us do its bidding

13
00:00:57,450 --> 00:00:59,530
has found its way into this city.

14
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:04,010
I am here for the purpose of recovering it.

15
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:08,080
He's trying to get information out of him
through this interchange, is he?

16
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,460
He's a first-rate adventurer, all right.

17
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:12,090
Demiur--

18
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:18,090
Ahem, Jaldabaoth, is there no other way
but for us to oppose each other?

19
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:20,600
No, there is not.

20
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:24,730
I realize that fairly well. In that event,

21
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:28,100
I will have to defeat you, right here.

22
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:30,860
You have no issue with that, do you?!

23
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:34,740
I am afraid I can't have that,
so I will have to resist.

24
00:01:34,990 --> 00:01:35,940
Here goes!

25
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:47,250
Amazing... What is that?

26
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,000
Is that...?

27
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,630
But my heart stopped 
beating a long time ago...

28
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:00,970
Hang in there, Lord Momon.

29
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:36,230
Miss Tuare, come, this way.

30
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,540
Are you all right?

31
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:43,570
Very well, let's get out of here while
Lord Sebas has the enemy drawn away.

32
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,290
Is something the matter, Lord Brain?

33
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:50,250
Hmm? Oh, no.

34
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:52,350
Let's go.

35
00:04:17,690 --> 00:04:18,900
Zero?!

36
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,510
That's right, kid.

37
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:28,330
I remember seeing your face before.
You're Brain Unglaus, right?

38
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:32,580
Which means that Succulent was beaten
because he was outmatched.

39
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:36,250
In recognition of your
extraordinary talent with the sword,

40
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:37,790
let me offer you a chance.

41
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,140
Kneel before me,

42
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:42,590
and swear that you will 
become my subordinate.

43
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:44,840
Do so, and I'll let you live.

44
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:50,260
Then you can die!

45
00:05:08,570 --> 00:05:11,630
Zero, I'll be the one to take you on.

46
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:15,150
Climb, I'll let you handle
the enemy to the rear.

47
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:17,630
You've got it.

48
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:22,130
Figured it out, did you?

49
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:24,300
The way you slipped around
behind me like you did,

50
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,630
anyone could have smelled a rat.

51
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:29,640
Although, I had my doubts
ever since I saw you in the cell.

52
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,810
Hmph, so it was all a cheap trick, eh?

53
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:36,690
Succulent, kill those two
small-timers behind you.

54
00:05:36,690 --> 00:05:38,400
You can at least do that, right?

55
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:41,190
O-Of course I can, Boss!

56
00:05:43,190 --> 00:05:44,650
We meet again, huh,

57
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:46,280
kid?

58
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:02,130
Hey, now. I hear that top-notch monks' fists
can become as hard as iron,

59
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:03,880
but this is beyond even that.

60
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:12,970
I'll back you up!

61
00:06:13,350 --> 00:06:15,980
This is the way a thief fights!

62
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,690
Poison?!

63
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,860
Powder of Will o' Wisp.

64
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:26,740
Thank you very much!

65
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:28,400
Damn it!

66
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:39,000
Martial Art! Ability Release!

67
00:06:57,890 --> 00:07:00,290
Hmph! Damn it, Succulent!

68
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:03,940
On the other hand, Unglaus,

69
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:06,030
you have done quite well.

70
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:10,570
You may be the first man to ever
withstand my attacks for as long as this.

71
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,640
As are you.

72
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:18,040
Then what if we were to start fighting
like we mean it just a bit?

73
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,580
That sounds good to me.

74
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:28,420
That thing you're doing
is a sword barrier, right?

75
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:31,970
If I am careless enough to step too close,
I'll be cut in half, won't I?

76
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:37,850
However, I can tell that
you can only do that technique

77
00:07:37,850 --> 00:07:39,810
by standing still, on the defensive.

78
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:47,690
Brain Unglaus, is that your ace in the hole?

79
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:49,590
That it is.

80
00:07:50,650 --> 00:07:53,110
A slashing attack uses both Field,
which never misses,

81
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:56,450
and my speed-of-god blade attack, God Flash.

82
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:59,140
Blade Technique, Whistling Wind!

83
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:04,120
I'm going to punch right through
that technique and hit you.

84
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:07,590
<i>I</i> am the strongest in the kingdom!

85
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,060
So this is where you are.

86
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:15,470
Wha--?! What is going on?

87
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:18,600
The other Six Arms were
supposed to be dealing with you!

88
00:08:18,850 --> 00:08:22,480
I have defeated all of your colleagues.

89
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:25,190
There's no way you could have
gone up against them

90
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:27,020
and come this far unharmed!

91
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:31,280
The truth is often taken
to be a surprising thing.

92
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:36,410
Lord Sebas, the Tuare that was
in the basement was a fake!

93
00:08:36,410 --> 00:08:37,910
We have to hurry and go save her!

94
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:44,420
Thank you very much for your concern.
However, it is all right.

95
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:52,320
Tuare, please wait here for a moment.

96
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:53,870
Right.

97
00:08:55,510 --> 00:09:00,440
Brain Unglaus, my fight with you
is on hold for now.

98
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:05,230
I'm going to show this old geezer
the power of Six Arms.

99
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:09,980
Geezer! You will pay for
these shenanigans with your life!

100
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:13,740
Panther!

101
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:14,940
Falcon!

102
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:17,740
Rhinoceros!

103
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:19,740
Buffalo!

104
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:21,740
Lion!

105
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:46,990
Wh-What are you...?

106
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:55,440
Whew, that was a close call.

107
00:09:56,280 --> 00:10:01,080
It would seem that I was just
the slightest bit stronger, though.

108
00:10:07,290 --> 00:10:10,540
Aspect of the Devil: Tentacle Wings!

109
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,530
Thank goodness you weren't hurt.

110
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,510
Y-Yeah...

111
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:29,450
Ah, your shoulder! Are you all right?!

112
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:34,060
Something this minor is no problem at all.

113
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:38,360
Never mind me,
I'm just relieved that you're all right.

114
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:45,120
Bravo. Imagine, being able
to keep her from any harm.

115
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:50,000
I, Jaldabaoth, would like
to sincerely offer you my praise.

116
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,540
I don't need your flattery.

117
00:10:55,210 --> 00:10:57,420
Wah! L-Lord Momon?!

118
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:59,930
Forgive me, bards of the world!

119
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:04,890
Knights do fight while defending
their delicate maidens in their arms!

120
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:09,980
This feels more like
being baggage than a princess...

121
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:13,610
No, no, this is no time
to be thinking anything so silly!

122
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:16,400
Well, I think it's time I be on my way.

123
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:19,900
Our objective is an item.

124
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:23,910
I will now encircle a section of
the capital city in the flames of hell.

125
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,700
If you make your way inside, I promise you,

126
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:31,960
purgatorial flames
will send you into the afterlife!

127
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:37,710
Th-This is bad, Lord Momon!
We have to get him, quickly!

128
00:11:37,710 --> 00:11:42,470
We can't. If we go after him,
he will start fighting like he really means it.

129
00:11:42,470 --> 00:11:43,680
If that happens...

130
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:48,180
Ah! Lord Momon, you're protecting me...

131
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:52,180
Okay then, what am I going to do <i>now</i>?

132
00:11:55,940 --> 00:12:00,190
So then, we drove the insect maid
right down to the ground.

133
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:01,950
You drove her?

134
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,450
And did you kill her?

135
00:12:08,450 --> 00:12:14,210
No, we didn't kill her.
Jaldabaoth showed up before we could.

136
00:12:14,210 --> 00:12:15,670
Is that right?

137
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:17,930
I see, I see--

138
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:26,260
Ahem! So um, couldn't it be
that Jaldabaoth got serious with you

139
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:29,260
because you were about 
to kill the insect maid?

140
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:31,990
We tugged on the tiger's tail
when we shouldn't have.

141
00:12:32,730 --> 00:12:34,440
That's what you're trying to say, right?

142
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,520
Jaldabaoth did say one thing--

143
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:40,990
He was going to envelop
part of the capital in hellfire.

144
00:12:40,990 --> 00:12:44,620
There's no way a maid that was
in his service is on the up-and-up.

145
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:50,400
I believe my friends were right
to challenge her to battle.

146
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:56,330
Er, yes... you're right.
What you're saying is correct.

147
00:12:56,850 --> 00:12:58,110
Pardon me.

148
00:12:58,110 --> 00:13:00,090
Ah, please, lift up your head!

149
00:13:00,090 --> 00:13:02,020
A man as handsome as you are shouldn't be...

150
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:08,970
Handsome?! What am I saying?!
Ah, but I can't help it, can I?

151
00:13:08,970 --> 00:13:10,970
It's okay for me to have girlish thoughts

152
00:13:10,970 --> 00:13:14,230
for the first time in hundreds of years,
isn't it? When he's this strong?

153
00:13:14,810 --> 00:13:18,400
Yes! He's a handsome warrior
who's even stronger than I am!

154
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,820
Miss Evileye?

155
00:13:20,610 --> 00:13:23,240
Y-Yes, um...

156
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:26,950
I need to discuss something with Nabe.
Excuse me a moment.

157
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:28,700
Huh?

158
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,270
She won't be able to hear us here.

159
00:13:33,950 --> 00:13:37,890
Nonetheless, we should still be cautious.

160
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,280
Now then, Nabe...

161
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:46,970
I can pretty well guess
what Demiurge's plan is, in large part.

162
00:13:46,970 --> 00:13:50,390
However, the more precise a machine is,

163
00:13:50,390 --> 00:13:52,600
the easier it is to make it all come apart

164
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,060
by throwing a monkey wrench in the gears.

165
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:56,980
We must prevent
the slightest misunderstanding

166
00:13:56,980 --> 00:14:00,390
from knocking everything back to square one.

167
00:14:00,390 --> 00:14:01,730
Do you know what I mean?

168
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:05,820
Indeed. I would expect no less
from the Supreme One.

169
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:08,360
I have everything well in hand.

170
00:14:08,950 --> 00:14:12,660
Like hell I do. I was called out here
in the first place by a request

171
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:15,370
from some grand nobleman
named Marquis Raeven.

172
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:19,400
We had to ride on a Floating Board,
and were carried along like luggage.

173
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:23,380
But, since the reward
was exceptional, that was fine.

174
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,880
And, because of
the disturbance here, I thought,

175
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,470
"This is the adventurer Momon's
first big fight in the capital city,

176
00:14:28,470 --> 00:14:31,640
so I have to make a cool entrance,"
and jumped down from there.

177
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:34,350
Ugh, how did things turn out this way?

178
00:14:38,890 --> 00:14:42,090
Now, I want you to get 
in touch with Demiurge.

179
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:46,900
The reason I don't do it myself
is that I can't use magic right now.

180
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:50,410
Also, I have that girl's eyes on me.

181
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:53,470
Hmph, she's watching.

182
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:57,660
She must have her doubts about me.

183
00:14:58,910 --> 00:15:01,630
You cannot mean it.
That is not the case, I daresay.

184
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:06,170
If I were to guess, could it not
be due to some other emotion?

185
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:12,300
Precisely why I <i>do</i> mean it. I can read
her thoughts like the back of my hand.

186
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:16,670
Becoming upset when she spoke
of Entoma was a critical mistake.

187
00:15:17,390 --> 00:15:19,480
I should have expected as much, Lord Ains.

188
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:24,110
Truly, your vision befits
one who sits upon the throne.

189
00:15:24,110 --> 00:15:25,550
Enough with the flattery.

190
00:15:26,190 --> 00:15:30,450
It's an obvious consideration
that arose from my own slip-up.

191
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:33,080
Now, let's get the ball rolling, Narberal.

192
00:15:33,530 --> 00:15:34,260
Yes, my lord.

193
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,180
Message.

194
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:45,590
That should keep my reputation
as the leader from falling apart.

195
00:15:46,170 --> 00:15:47,590
Now then...

196
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:54,180
You know, it's hard to believe
that a little child like that

197
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:56,710
possesses adamantite class strength.

198
00:15:58,850 --> 00:16:00,600
Sorry to keep you waiting.

199
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:03,560
Would you like me to help you carry them?

200
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:06,860
My friends should be along shortly.

201
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:12,240
It's possible that we will be able
to cast resurrection magic right here.

202
00:16:12,570 --> 00:16:17,280
Ho, you have someone
that can use resurrection magic?

203
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:24,040
Oh, uh, yes. Our team leader,
Lakyus, can invoke Raise Dead,

204
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:26,000
which is a 5th tier spell.

205
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,510
Will they be able to engage in combat
right after they return to life?

206
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:32,300
I'm afraid not.

207
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:37,640
This magic costs a huge amount
of life force at the time of resurrection.

208
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:39,240
Ho-ho...

209
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:44,140
As such, they won't be able to
physically move about very well for a while.

210
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:46,560
So much so that when it's cast
on those with lower life forces,

211
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:49,250
they will be reduced to ashes,
so it can't be used.

212
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:55,030
I see. If you wouldn't mind,
could we wait here with you?

213
00:16:55,030 --> 00:16:57,990
I would like to meet this woman, Lakyus.

214
00:16:57,990 --> 00:17:00,660
Wh-Why do you want to meet Lakyus?!

215
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,530
Sure enough, she's acting wary.

216
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:08,250
Well, um, I would like to meet
the leader of the Blue Rose,

217
00:17:08,250 --> 00:17:10,460
a fellow adventurer,
and my senior in experience.

218
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:12,420
Is there some reason why I should not?

219
00:17:13,130 --> 00:17:16,490
N-No! No, there's no problem!

220
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:17,930
Mr. Momon...

221
00:17:18,470 --> 00:17:20,040
...please look over there.

222
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:44,070
What will you do after this, Lord Sebas?

223
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:47,640
I will take Tuare to a safe location,

224
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:50,460
to make sure that
nothing like this ever happens again.

225
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:56,220
Very well. Lord Sebas, thank you
for what you've done these last two nights.

226
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:58,680
Please do not let it concern you.

227
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:04,480
Someday, I will repay the debt
I owe you for helping to save her.

228
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,600
A wall of flame?

229
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:49,550
What is that?

230
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:51,900
The flames of Gehenna?

231
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,990
My good adventurers,

232
00:19:01,990 --> 00:19:06,390
thank you for coming together
in this time of crisis.

233
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:13,920
Early this morning, a wall of flame
sprang up around this area of the capital.

234
00:19:14,710 --> 00:19:17,420
These flames are similar to an illusion,

235
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:20,000
and coming into contact with them
seems to do no harm.

236
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:25,430
The leader of the Blue Rose
has in fact confirmed this.

237
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,640
I actually touched it.

238
00:19:29,230 --> 00:19:31,100
I didn't feel the least bit of heat,

239
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:34,730
and went inside without 
any interference at all.

240
00:19:34,730 --> 00:19:38,650
I also confirmed that there are low-level
demons on the other side of the wall.

241
00:19:40,950 --> 00:19:44,870
The ringleader behind this incident
is named Jaldabaoth.

242
00:19:44,870 --> 00:19:47,910
We have information that he is
an extremely fiendish and powerful demon,

243
00:19:47,910 --> 00:19:51,830
who has many other evil entities serving him.

244
00:19:52,670 --> 00:19:54,250
Just how strong is he?

245
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:58,050
Two of my comrades,
the warrior Gagaran and the thief Tia,

246
00:19:58,050 --> 00:20:00,260
were killed by him.

247
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:02,380
And it only took him one blow, at that.

248
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:04,390
--What?!
--One blow?!

249
00:20:04,390 --> 00:20:05,480
Don't lose your heads!

250
00:20:06,510 --> 00:20:09,140
Jaldabaoth is strong, to be sure.

251
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:10,810
As someone who actually confronted him,

252
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:13,300
and was powerless to stop him,
I can assure you of that.

253
00:20:14,150 --> 00:20:17,280
However, we have this man on our side!

254
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,930
The Raven Black Hero, Master Momon!

255
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:29,660
Yes. We are absolutely not going
into a fight that we cannot win.

256
00:20:30,450 --> 00:20:33,320
Now, allow me to present
our detailed plan of attack...

257
00:20:41,550 --> 00:20:44,550
Lastly, we will need a detached force
to rescue the civilians

258
00:20:44,550 --> 00:20:48,260
who are trapped inside the wall of flame.

259
00:20:50,810 --> 00:20:53,570
If the demons are holding them captive,

260
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:57,060
they will likely use one of
the warehouse districts inside the wall.

261
00:20:57,440 --> 00:21:00,820
They'll split up families,
to keep them from breaking out.

262
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,810
Climb, you'll go, right?

263
00:21:09,990 --> 00:21:13,270
As you wish. Even if it costs my life.

264
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:15,740
Princess,

265
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:18,440
would it be okay if I went along, too?

266
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:22,240
Are you sure, Lord Brain Unglaus?

267
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:26,340
Well, count me in, too.

268
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:31,180
All right, everyone, I will remain here,

269
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:36,350
praying to God that
every last one of you comes back.

270
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:37,670
Good hunting!

271
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:41,860
Leave it to us!

272
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:44,610
Long live the Golden Princess!

273
00:21:46,490 --> 00:21:47,360
Climb...

274
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,120
I'll lend you this.

275
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,540
What is it?

276
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:54,250
A magic item?

277
00:21:54,250 --> 00:22:00,630
Yeah. It's supposed to raise one's power
as a warrior well past their limits.

278
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:03,010
Past their limits?

279
00:22:03,010 --> 00:22:06,260
I-I can't accept such a precious item!

280
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:09,760
I myself got it from an old lady I know.

281
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:12,310
Bring it back to me alive.

282
00:22:15,390 --> 00:22:18,640
We all have to come back,
for the princess's sake.

283
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:21,800
Right!

284
00:22:30,740 --> 00:22:33,910
Form a line using the adventurers,

285
00:22:33,910 --> 00:22:38,380
and have the guardsmen back them up,
to thin out the enemy's formation...

286
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:41,130
Then have the greatest force,

287
00:22:41,130 --> 00:22:46,220
consisting of the raven-black Momon
and Nabe, as well as Evileye,

288
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:49,160
acting as an arrowhead
to break through the enemy's center.

289
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:52,740
But isn't Climb's mission a dangerous one?

290
00:22:53,810 --> 00:22:56,520
He will be making rounds inside the capital,

291
00:22:56,520 --> 00:23:00,170
together with your soldiers, won't he?
It will be no different for him.

292
00:23:03,070 --> 00:23:05,150
Climb may end up dead,

293
00:23:05,650 --> 00:23:09,780
but if he does, Lakyus will cast
her resurrection magic on him.

294
00:23:09,990 --> 00:23:13,330
Then, when his life force
is drawn out by the magic,

295
00:23:13,330 --> 00:23:16,640
who will look after the weakened Climb?

296
00:23:18,410 --> 00:23:20,580
Who could object to nursing back to health

297
00:23:20,580 --> 00:23:25,740
someone who followed orders to his death,
and then came back to life?

298
00:23:26,380 --> 00:23:27,590
So that's it.

299
00:23:27,590 --> 00:23:31,050
All according to plan, my sister?

300
00:23:32,510 --> 00:23:33,050
Yes.

301
00:23:33,050 --> 00:23:35,050


